{
  "chapter": "STEAM_AGE",
  "description": "Ah yes, §3steam§r. A wonderful source of power that uses the pressure and heat of steam to move machinery to further increase the power of technology. With the buff to GregTech steam, it is now even easier to use your steam to power all those delightful §6steam multiblocks§r.

§aGreg Solid Boilers§r: Use solid burnable fuels to produce steam. These are the easiest to fuel; just grab some logs or coal, and you can get quite a decent amount of steam from coal.

§aGreg Liquid Boilers§r: Use lava or creosote to make steam. Creosote can be obtained nicely from the §8coke oven§r. Below are the best fuels to sustain your creosote production:

coal => can sustain 8 HPLB
logs => can sustain 4 HPLB However, I do not suggest running liquid boilers because of the fast production of sugarcane from sand.

---



§aGreg Solar Boilers§r: Use the power of the sun to provide heat for your steam production. These are quite nice as they are passive steam during the day but have a higher initial investment than solid or liquid boilers.",
